From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blackhat-7 <44942105+blackhat-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:07:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 28/33] NVIDIA helper: review fixes

- One NVIDIA tier only: the plugin keeps one card's state, so a second tier (--expert-cache-device2/3) is refused
  instead of taking the first one's.
- The NVIDIA code (dlopen, the AVX2 q8_1 quantizer) builds only for a HIP engine on x86-64 Linux; elsewhere
  STRATA_NV_HELPER is an error.
- dispatch reads the layer's native format only on the NVIDIA path (non-native layouts have none).
- The 4070's adaptive swaps run after the primary's, so `pending` holds this round's swaps: the helper no longer
  loads an expert the primary is loading in the same round.
- --adapt-async 1 is refused beside the helper (its landing step runs in the blocking tier only).
- Swap fills read blob_stable(): the copy runs after the call returns.
- The deferred launch (pool pre-drain hook) and the tail-skip change apply only with the NVIDIA helper; other
  helpers keep the old order and rules.
- The fused gate/up + SwiGLU kernel is turned on by the plugin through a setter (STRATA_GU_SWIGLU still decides
  first); the CUDA engine's own sm_89 default is unchanged again.
- RemoteMeta moves to remote_meta.hpp, shared by the engine and the plugin (was a copy).
- The timing split prints at close, not from the gpu_ms getter; dead code removed; --as-needed for the plugin.
